nio: mark the steps inside bsd_utaskbootstrap

The checkpoints of run 596 show "CHK after siginit" but not
"CHK after utaskbootstrap", so the boot is stuck inside
bsd_utaskbootstrap(), which clones the init process with
cloneproc().  That call allocates a process and a thread; one
of those steps is not coming back, but there is no mark to say
which.

Put direct-to-framebuffer marks before and after cloneproc()
and after proc_find(1).  The next photograph will name the exact
step that blocks.  No behaviour changes.

diff --git a/bsd/kern/bsd_init.c b/bsd/kern/bsd_init.c
index 961ad9e..03e112c 100644
--- a/bsd/kern/bsd_init.c
+++ b/bsd/kern/bsd_init.c
@@ -1432,9 +1432,12 @@ bsd_utaskbootstrap(void)
 	 * Clone the bootstrap process from the kernel process, without
 	 * inheriting either task characteristics or memory from the kernel;
 	 */
+	nio_bmark("\nnio: UT pre-cloneproc");
 	thread = cloneproc(TASK_NULL, NULL, kernproc, CLONEPROC_FLAGS_MEMSTAT_INTERNAL);
+	nio_bmark("\nnio: UT post-cloneproc");
 
 	/* Hold the reference as it will be dropped during shutdown */
+	nio_bmark("\nnio: UT post-procfind");
 	initproc = proc_find(1);
 #if __PROC_INTERNAL_DEBUG
 	if (initproc == PROC_NULL) {
